--output-format stream-json now reports when a configured MCP or OpenAPI server failed to connect, and it's committed as 297c2ab1. Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass. The unit tests call the helper directly; I didn't run yoyo end to end against a server that really fails.

What changed: before this, stream-json only passed along the agent's own events, so a script reading it couldn't tell a degraded run from a healthy one. Now, if at least one server failed, one extra line comes after the final agentEnd event:

```
{"type":"externalServers","mcp_connected":1,"mcp_failed":["npx some-server"],"openapi_connected":0,"openapi_failed":[]}
```

• **Same fields as the json output:** the line is built by the existing external_servers_json plus a type field, so there's no second serializer.
• **Healthy runs are unchanged:** the line only appears when something failed. With every server connected, or none configured, the output is byte-for-byte what it was before.
• **The first line is still agentStart:** the extra line is printed only after the event stream ends.
• **The model still gets its warning:** the line reads the stored report without consuming it, so the note the model sees on its first turn is left alone. A test checks this.

Where the code is: the helper, the print function and 5 tests are in a new file, src/prompt/stream_external_servers.rs. Both stream-json entry points in src/prompt.rs call it right after the event loop returns. I put the call there rather than inside handle_stream_json_events because unit tests drive that handler directly and other tests write failures into the shared report.

Tests:
• An empty report, and a report with only successful connections, produce no line.
• An MCP failure names mcp and the server.
• An OpenAPI failure reports openapi, not mcp.
• The line's fields equal the json output's object plus type.

I also broke the empty check on purpose and confirmed empty_report_emits_nothing failed, then restored it and saw it pass.

Docs: docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md now describes the line: when it appears, its shape, and that it's missing on healthy runs. I also fixed its old "the last line is always agentEnd" sentence, which this change makes false. ARCHITECTURE.md has a new entry under prompt.rs, and the size-gate register entry for src/prompt.rs now reads 3790 lines (was 3785).

• **Run not marked as an error:** a degraded run still isn't flagged as an error, matching how the json output behaves. A script has to look for this line.
• Extra commits: there are two work-in-progress commits before the final one.
